e{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(\\pi ,-\\pi ).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381258 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ba29a24e-25aa-5034-8849-e753260af75f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381258 #edb/ref 1074 "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}) & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)}{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)}{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(\\pi ,-\\pi ):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(\\pi ,-\\pi )} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\pi )}{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi ))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(-1)(-1)}{(-1-0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381259 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381260 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381259 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381261 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381259 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381262 #edb/ref 